# Design System (Component Library)

**Framework-first:** compose UI from `@design-system` before inventing feature-local controls. The live catalogue is `/` (`DesignSystemShowcase`). The written catalogue is `src/framework/design-system/README.md`.

Angular `app-*` selectors map to PascalCase React components exported from `@design-system` (see mapping table below).

## Import rule

```tsx
import { Button, Input, PageLayout, H1, P, Callout, RoutedModal } from '@design-system';
```

Never import with deep relative paths into `src/framework/design-system/`. Re-export new public components from `src/framework/design-system/index.ts`.

## Catalogue (current public API)

| Component | Use for | Key props |
|-----------|---------|-----------|
| `Button` | All actions (not raw `<button>`) | `theme`, `loading`, `circle`, `buttonSize`, `fullWidth`, `tid`, `disabled` |
| `Input` | Text / number / date fields | `label`, `hideLabel`, `requiredField`, `hint`, `error`, `inputSize`, `tid` |
| `PasswordInput` | Password fields | same pattern as `Input` + show/hide |
| `FormField`, `FormFieldLabel`, `FormFieldError` | Compose custom controls with shared label/error chrome | `tid`, `requiredField`, `error` |
| `Checkbox` | Boolean checkbox | `label`, `tid`, standard input attrs |
| `Switch` | On/off toggle (`role="switch"`) | `label`, `tid`, `checked`, `readOnly` |
| `Badge` | Small count / tag chip | `children` |
| `PageLayout` | Page shell | `header`, `children`, `footer` |
| `H1`, `H2`, `H3`, `P` | Typography (not bare headings/paragraphs with custom classes) | `H3` has `variant?: 'default' \| 'section'` |
| `Callout` | Inline alerts | `type: 'info' \| 'success' \| 'warning' \| 'error'` |
| `Icon` | Spec icon glyphs | `name: IconName`, `size` (default `1.8rem`) |
| `Modal` | Imperative / local dialog portal | `open`, `onClose`, `size`, `presentation`, `level`, `allowKeyboardClose`, `tid`, `ariaLabel` |
| `ModalShell` | Title / body / footer chrome inside a modal | `title`, `onClose`, `loading`, `formErrors`, `footerRight`, `tid` |
| `RoutedModal` | Feature create/edit/view modals tied to route dismiss | `title`, `tid`, `dismissHref`, `preferBackOnClose`, `size`, `level`, `loading`, `formErrors`, `closeLabel`, `footerRight` |
| `ConfirmModal` | Confirm / cancel prompt | see component props |
| `DropdownMenu` | Actions / overflow menus (portalled, never clipped) | `items`, `renderTrigger(triggerProps)`, `align`, `onTriggerIntent`, `tid` |
| `ThemeProvider`, `useTheme` | Light/dark via `html[data-theme]` | wrap app shell |

Hooks (also from `@design-system`):

- `useModalDismiss(dismissHref, preferBackOnClose?)` — close routed modal
- `useModalNavigate()` — `open(href)` for parallel-route modals
- `useModalPreload(href, preload?)` — warm a routed modal from its opening page (see `nextjs-modal-routing.mdc`)

Types: `ButtonTheme`, `ButtonProps`, `InputProps`, `ModalSize`, `ModalPresentation`, `ModalLevel`, `CalloutType`, `IconName`.

## Angular → React name map

| Angular | React (`@design-system`) |
|---------|--------------------------|
| `app-button` | `Button` |
| `app-input` (and similar form controls) | `Input`, `PasswordInput`, `Checkbox`, `Switch` |
| `app-form-label` | `FormFieldLabel` / `Input` `label` |
| `app-h1` … `app-h5`, `app-p` | `H1`, `H2`, `H3`, `P` (extend typography as needed) |
| `app-page-layout` slots `[header]`/`[body]`/`[footer]` | `PageLayout` props `header` / `children` / `footer` |
| `app-callout` | `Callout` |
| `app-icon` | `Icon` |
| `app-badge` | `Badge` |
| Form modal template | `RoutedModal` + `ModalShell` |
| MatDialog blade/dialog | `Modal` `presentation: 'dialog' \| 'blade'` |

Not yet ported (prefer extend `@design-system` when needed): charts, loaders, tab-list, slide-out-only shells, view-card-layout, dataset-select as standalone. JSON Forms renderers live under `@json-schema-form`, not raw design-system forks.

## Button conventions

```tsx
<Button theme="primary-action" tid="save-item" loading={inFlight} onClick={onSave}>
  Save
</Button>
<Button theme="secondary-action" tid="cancel-item" onClick={onCancel}>
  Cancel
</Button>
```

`ButtonTheme`: `'primary-action' | 'secondary-action' | 'system-red' | 'system-green' | 'alternate'`.

- Default `type="button"` (set `type="submit"` only inside forms that need it).
- `loading` disables the button and shows the overlay spinner.
- Destructive confirm actions use `theme="system-red"`.

## Form controls

- Prefer `Input` / `Checkbox` / `Switch` / `PasswordInput` for manual forms (e.g. sign-in, showcase).
- Entity create/edit that has a server JSON schema uses `@json-schema-form` (`JsonSchemaForm`) — do **not** hand-build field lists that duplicate the schema. See `nextjs-json-schema-forms.mdc`.
- Pass `tid` on interactive controls; `Input` renders `data-tid` on the input and `data-tid="{tid}-field"` on the wrapper.
- Surface field errors via the `error` prop (or `FormFieldError`); do not invent parallel error UI.

## Typography & layout

```tsx
<PageLayout
  header={
    <>
      <H1>Page title</H1>
      <P>Supporting description.</P>
    </>
  }
>
  {/* body */}
</PageLayout>
```

Use `H1`–`H3` and `P` instead of bare `<h1>` / `<p>` with one-off classes. Section labels in showcases use `<H3 variant="section">`.

## Callouts & feedback

```tsx
<Callout type="error">{message}</Callout>
```

Use for page/modal-level messages. Field-level messages stay on the control.

## Modals (component API)

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Feature form opened by URL (grid Add/Edit) | `RoutedModal` |
| Local demo / non-routed dialog | `Modal` + `ModalShell` |
| Delete / confirm | `ConfirmModal` |

`ModalSize`: `'responsive' | 'small' | 'large' | 'extraLarge'`.  
`ModalPresentation`: `'dialog'` (default) | `'blade'`.  
`ModalLevel`: `'primary' | 'secondary' | 'tertiary'` (stacking).

Set `allowKeyboardClose={false}` when matching Angular form-modal behaviour that blocks Esc/backdrop dismiss during edit, if the product requires it.

## Composition & state

- Design-system components are presentational or lightly stateful (controlled inputs via props). Feature orchestration (load, save, permissions) stays in feature hooks / data providers.
- Client components that use hooks or browser APIs start with `'use client'`.
- Prefer controlled form values (`value` + `onChange`) when wiring to entity form state.
- Theme: wrap the app with `ThemeProvider`; toggle via `useTheme().toggleTheme`. Theme attribute is `html[data-theme='light'|'dark']`.

## Styling inside the library

- Co-locate `{Name}.module.css` beside `{Name}.tsx`.
- Colours and surfaces come from `theme/tokens.css` CSS variables (`--primary-action`, `--app-*`, `--ink-*`). Do not introduce new hardcoded hex when a token exists.
- `html { font-size: 62.5%; }` — size with **rem** (1rem ≈ 10px).
- Dark mode: rely on semantic tokens that already flip under `html[data-theme='dark']`.
- Menus / popovers: use `DropdownMenu` (portal to `<body>` + `--z-index-popover`). Do not hand-roll `position: absolute` menus inside tables or modals, and do not remove `overflow` on grid / modal wrappers to un-clip them.

## Adding a new design-system component

1. Create folder under the right group: `buttons/`, `forms/`, `layout/`, `components/`, `typography/`, `theme/`.
2. Files: `ComponentName.tsx`, `ComponentName.module.css` (if styled).
3. Export props interface; accept optional `tid?: string` on interactive elements and set `data-tid={tid}`.
4. Export from `src/framework/design-system/index.ts`.
5. Document in `src/framework/design-system/README.md` and add a section (or controls) to `DesignSystemShowcase` when the control is user-visible.
6. There is no Storybook in this Next.js repo yet; the showcase page is the visual contract.

